{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments ["And the reason for <b>\"If the children of Gad and the children of Reuben pass over, etc., you shall give them the land of Gilead as a possession\"</b> is that now Moses had not handed over to them all the land of Sihon and Og, but only some cities in the land of Gilead, which is a place for livestock — namely Atroth and Dibon and those mentioned here (Numbers 32:34–38), in which they built fortified cities for their little ones and their cattle to dwell in. And the rest of the land they left desolate. Therefore he commanded Joshua and the princes: if they pass over with you, give them the entire land as an everlasting possession; and if they do not wish to pass over with you, take from them all this land and drive out their wives and their little ones from there, and give them a possession suited to them in the land of Canaan that they will conquer for themselves there when they cross over there. And Rabbi Abraham said (Ibn Ezra on Numbers 32:30): and if they do not pass over willingly, you shall lead them with you by force and they shall take possession there among you."], :book :numbers, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {0 "Ramban here paraphrases Ibn Ezra's comment rather than quoting it verbatim; the gist and reference are preserved as he gives them."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:10:01.271046914Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}